{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18030 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "Ustusol A is implicated in the biological activity toward HepG2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ustusol A acts as a target for multiple entities, including MOVP-3 and Cocosamide B, which in turn target HepG2. This indicates that Ustusol A may exert its effects by modulating the activity of these intermediaries, which are themselves targets of the compound 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. The shared involvement of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One in targeting HepG2 suggests a potential mechanism where Ustusol A may influence the expression or function of these intermediaries, ultimately leading to effects on HepG2 cells. The evidence is consistent with a pathway where Ustusol A serves as a bridge to the downstream targets, highlighting a possible role in modulating cellular responses in HepG2.",
